<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Partition of Poland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1772">1772</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as First Partition</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Partition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in 1772 was the annexation of large parts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. It reduced the Commonwealth's territory and population substantially and began the process that ended with its complete disappearance in 1795.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-partition-of-poland.jpg" alt="First Partition of Poland" width="320" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Mathiasrex, Maciej Szczepańczyk, vased on layers of User:Halibutt · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Polish-Lithuanian_Commonwealth_1773-1789.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
